ell des Panzers VI \"Panther\" Ausf. F mit Schmalturm.","license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5","attribution":"Darkone"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Warsaw_Uprising_by_Deczkowki_-_Wacek_Platoon_-_15911.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Warsaw_Uprising_by_Deczkowki_-_Wacek_Platoon_-_15911.jpg","width":960,"height":635,"caption":"WarsawUprising: Soldiers of tank platoon \"Wacek\" of \"Zośka\" Battalion on a German Panther tank around Okopowa Street. Sitting from the left: Zdzisław Moszczeński \"Ryk\" [2] (according to source [1] „Ryk” is standing first from left facing the tank), unknown, Jan Uniewski „Lumeński\" [2] („Łuniewski” a","license":"Public domain","attribution":"Juliusz Bogdan Deczkowski"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Captured_Axis_Vehicles_PzV.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Captured_Axis_Vehicles_PzV.jpg","width":953,"height":586,"caption":"A captured Panzerkampfwagen V in Red Army use.","license":"Public domain","attribution":"unkrown"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Panther_CanadianWarMuseum.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panther_CanadianWarMuseum.jpg","width":900,"height":600,"caption":"Panther Ausf. A at the Canadian War Museum, Ottawa. August 2008.","license":"Public domain","attribution":"Markbruinekreeft"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9c/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-J14589%2C_Albert_Speer%2C_Panzer_T-34.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-J14589,_Albert_Speer,_Panzer_T-34.jpg","width":596,"height":783,"caption":"For documentary purposes the German Federal Archive often retained the original image captions, which may be erroneous, biased, obsolete or politically extreme. Albert Speer, Panzer T-34\nDer Reichsminister für Bewaffnung und Munition [Albert] S